 R←Test_Misc_013(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;parms;cmd
⍝ Exercise `PrintReleaseCommand`. Everything is made up, so nothing is collected and
⍝ nothing is sent anywhere: the function just builds the command line.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '∘∘∘ ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 parms←⎕NS''
 parms.owner←'aplteam'
 parms.repo←'TestRepo'
 parms.tag←'v9.9.9'
 parms.releaseTitle←'Version 9.9.9'
 parms.body←⍬                                 ⍝ No notes, so no temp file is created
 parms.projectHome←'C:/nonsense'
 parms.assets←'Dist/rel.zip'('C:/elsewhere/abs.zip')   ⍝ One relative, one absolute
 parms.draft←1
 parms.prerelease←0
 parms.target←''
 parms.missing←⍬

 cmd←##.GitHub.PrintReleaseCommand parms
 →T.PassesIf∨/'gh release create "v9.9.9"'⍷cmd
 →T.PassesIf∨/'--repo "aplteam/TestRepo"'⍷cmd
 →T.PassesIf∨/'--title "Version 9.9.9"'⍷cmd
 →T.PassesIf∨/'--draft'⍷cmd
 →T.PassesIf~∨/'--prerelease'⍷cmd             ⍝ Not a pre-release, so the flag must be absent
 →T.PassesIf~∨/'--notes-file'⍷cmd             ⍝ No notes were collected
 →T.PassesIf∨/'"C:/nonsense/Dist/rel.zip"'⍷cmd        ⍝ Resolved against projectHome
 →T.PassesIf∨/'"C:/elsewhere/abs.zip"'⍷cmd            ⍝ Absolute, so left alone

 R←T._OK
⍝Done
